Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.409
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.134 --> 00:00:07.550
SPEAKER: Keeping tabs on your
apps and dealing with errors

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.340
can involve multiple tools
from multiple vendors.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.350
This is far from
ideal, and you really

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:15.290
want all the tools
you need in one place.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.570
Stackdriver monitoring
provides visibility

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.150
into the performance,
uptime, and overall health

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.550
of cloud-powered applications.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.920
Stackdriver collects
metrics, events, and metadata

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.040
from Google Cloud Platform,
Amazon Web Services,

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.010
posted uptime probes,
application instrumentation,

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.800
and a variety of common
application components,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.790
including Cassandra,
Nginx, Apache Web Server,

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.140
and many others.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.450
Stackdriver ingests
that data and generates

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.420
insights via dashboards,
charts, and alerts.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.670
Stackdriver alerting
helps you collaborate

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:50.030
by integrating with
Slack, PagerDuty, HipChat,

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.850
Campfire, and more.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.830
This hands-on lab shows you
how to monitor a Google Compute

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:57.470
Engine virtual machine
instance with Stackdriver.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:00.620
You'll also install monitoring
and logging agents for your VM

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.410
which collects more information
from your instance, which

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:06.316
could include metrics and
logs from third-party apps.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:08.690
By the end of the lab, you'll
have successfully monitored

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:11.570
a virtual machine and checked
the logs it generated.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:15.200
Next up on our quest is Cloud
Functions, Qwik Start console.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.550
[MUSIC PLAYING]

